SUMMARY:Do Neural Networks Have World Models?
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Speaker: John Morrison\, Professor of Philosophy\, Barnard Coll
 ege\, Columbia UniversityTalk Abstract: It is often claimed that neural ne
 tworks build internal "world models." But the term is used in many conflic
 ting ways\, and the evidence offered for it is rarely examined. This talk 
 has two parts. First\, drawing on joint work with Raphaël Millière\, I p
 ropose a minimal notion of a world model: a single\, unified representatio
 n of a task that preserves its structural relations. I explain how this no
 tion sits within a hierarchy of stronger ones\, and argue
